# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` ships ~845 MB of junk into the image: two
# virtualenvs, every teacher-uploaded PDF under storage/, and the git history.
# venv311/ is a WINDOWS virtualenv — copying it into a python:3.11-slim
# container is not merely wasteful, its binaries cannot run there at all.
#
# Keep in mind what the runtime actually needs: app/, main.py, admin_main.py,
# migrations/ + alembic.ini (alembic upgrade runs in the container),
# requirements.txt, setup_db.py. Everything else is build-time or local-only.

# Virtualenvs (venv311/ = 660 MB, venv/ = 26 MB)
venv/
venv311/
.venv/

# Runtime data — bind-mounted by docker-compose, never baked in.
# The Dockerfile's own `mkdir -p storage/...` recreates the empty tree.
storage/
temp_images/
logs/

# VCS and local tooling
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/

# Python bytecode / caches
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Tests and docs — not needed to run the bot
tests/
docs/
*.md

# Secrets must never enter an image layer. .env is gitignored, but the build
# context is the filesystem, not git — without this line it would be copied.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The AI-text detector is its own image (detector/Dockerfile, build context
# ./detector). The bot only talks to it over HTTP and never imports it; its
# virtualenv (~1.5 GB with torch) and model files (hundreds of MB) must never
# reach the bot/admin/online image.
detector/
